{"resourceIdentifier":"2538","resourceName":"Pendjari and W-Benin National Parks REDD+ Project","description":"The Pendjari and W-Benin National Parks REDD+ project, implements measures orientated to protect the natural ecosystems in the parks and the adjacent hunting zones (Djona, Mekrou, Batia, Porga, Seri). Such actions are focused on preventing the main drivers of deforestation and conversion in the project area. These activities provide new opportunities to change the agents’ behaviour and are as follow:\r\n●\tEngagement with local communities and management of regional transhumance and local pastoralism across the Parks\r\n●\tSupport of educational activities, providing school material, school grants and free visits to the local students.\r\n●\tThe establishment of more sustainable practices\r\n●\tIncreasement of employment opportunities and Implementations of sustainable Income Generating Activities (IGAs) throughout certain zones of the parks\r\n●\tTraining and equipping rangers, for maintaining control over the project area, enforcing the law, and protecting forest and grassland areas from illegal human intervention.\r\nThe implementation of these activities increases the protection of the ecosystem by reducing the human pressure for natural resources while generating additional incomes for ensuring the long-term funding of the park and employment opportunities for local communities.\r\nAlthough the project area itself is a national protected area, regardless of its uninhabited, the savanna ecosystems and forests in the project area have faced different threats that put their long-term conservation at risk. Such threats include the following:\r\n●\tPressure from the surrounding communities for agricultural land (self-consumption and cash crops),\r\n●\tconflict among transhumant communities and sedentary ones for resources (land for crops and for feeding cattle), \r\n●\tdeforestation for producing firewood and charcoal.","location":{"latitude":11.299720,"longitude":1.960277},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2025-03-15","endExclusive":"2025-04-15","endInclusive":"2025-04-14"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2538"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"African Parks Benin (A Branch of African Parks Network)"},{"type":"string","value":"Johannesburg, South Africa"},{"type":"string","value":"+31650274566"},{"type":"string","value":"info@africanparks.org"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2538"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2538"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"228923"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":63817}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"REDD"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0009"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1214239 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AENOR CONFIA, S.A. (UNIPERSONAL)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"05/10/2023"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 24/08/2017 - 23/08/2047"}]}]},{"programCode":"CCB","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"African Parks Benin (A Branch of African Parks Network)"},{"type":"string","value":"Johannesburg, South Africa"},{"type":"string","value":"+31650274566"},{"type":"string","value":"info@africanparks.org"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification public comment period expired"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_E